{:adr-id "2627000000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-7740 (leasing of intellectual property and similar products, except copyrighted works) IP-leasing-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500" "ADR-2607121200"]
 :mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-5913 (filmdistops.* module shape, Wave 4 verified sibling actor)"

 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 7740 = leasing of intellectual property and similar products,
  EXCEPT copyrighted works -- patents, trademarks, franchise rights;
  copyrighted works (books/music/film) are covered by different ISIC
  classes. Live registry.edn :name for \"7740\" independently verified
  fresh: truncated \"Leasing of intellectual property and similar
  products, exce...\" (pre-existing seed-data truncation bug, ~10% of
  entries), unambiguously matching the target class. A separate,
  redundant 3-digit group entry {:id \"774\" ...} with a similarly
  truncated name sits at :maturity :spec and was deliberately left
  untouched, per this fleet's caution against conflating class-level and
  group-level registry entries. No existing repo at
  cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7740 (404) or at the registry's
  placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-N7740, itself bogus -- wrong
  org/id-shape, never real). Fresh scaffold, not a repair. IP leasing
  touches licensing-grant and royalty-rate-determination decisions --
  per ADR-2607152500's Wave4 guardrail, closed op allowlist must never
  include an op that directly finalizes either; any 'flag concern' op
  always escalates, never auto-commit-eligible."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a licensing grant (who is licensed to practice a patent, use a trademark, or operate a franchise, under what terms) -- hard, permanent block"
  "finalizing a royalty-rate determination (locking in what rate a licensee actually pays) -- hard, permanent block"
  "license-agreement negotiation, contract drafting, binding execution -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known bug class this batch repeatedly hit: bare-noun scope-excluded-terms
  (e.g. 'license', 'royalty') self-match inside the mock advisor's own
  legitimate default rationale text, self-blocking the actor's happy path
  -- especially acute here since :log-license-record/
  :coordinate-royalty-reporting routinely disclaim 'not a licensing-grant
  decision'/'not a royalty-rate decision' in their own default rationale,
  and :flag-infringement-concern's entire purpose is to discuss
  licensing/infringement topics using exactly those bare nouns. Fix:
  scope-excluded-terms phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION
  ('finalize the licensing grant', 'set the royalty rate', 'grant the
  license', JP equivalents), never a bare noun -- verified from the start
  via a pre-write substring-collision scan of every default advisor
  rationale/summary string against the full term list (zero collisions),
  then independently confirmed by the dedicated regression test
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in
  governor_test.clj, which asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for
  a clean registered+verified license record, never trip :scope-excluded
  and never HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-7740 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/
  Operation/Sim, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5913's filmdistops.* module
  shape module-for-module as ipleaseops.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed licenses directory
    (license-id/name/registered?/verified?), append-only ledger +
    licensing-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-license-record, schedule-review-operation, flag-infringement-concern,
    coordinate-royalty-reporting
  - Governor (IPLeaseGovernor): 2 named HARD checks (license-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check
    (finalize-licensing-grant / finalize-royalty-rate-determination /
    closed 4-op allowlist). always-escalate-ops #{:flag-infringement-concern},
    confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-license-record only, approval;
    phase2 += schedule-review-operation/coordinate-royalty-reporting,
    approval; phase3 auto-commits those 3 when clean+confident;
    flag-infringement-concern never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval},
    NOT a stub -- mirrors filmdistops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow + all
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory
    self-trip regression), phase_test, governor_contract_test -- 40 tests /
    119 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. README/
    GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT written fresh for this
    domain"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 7740 IP-leasing-operations-coordination genuinely implemented and
    fully tested"
   "licensing-grant and royalty-rate-determination exclusions hardcoded in
    governor checks (scope-exclusion-violations), not just README prose"
   "self-trip bug class fixed by construction (action-phrased terms,
    pre-write collision scan) + covered by dedicated regression test, not
    avoided by luck"
   "flag-infringement-concern always-escalate is a two-layer invariant
    (governor always-escalate-ops + phase's permanent absence from every
    :auto set)"
   "portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs; clojure -M:lint 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests use
    in-memory MemStore, matching every sibling actor's current maturity"
   "mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor protocol seam
    ready for that swap but not wired in this ADR"]}

